From: CoolFreeze23 <34906576+CoolFreeze23@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: cancel reset work also on the QMI failure remove path

ath12k_pci_remove() and ath12k_ahb_remove() jump straight to
ath12k_core_deinit() when ATH12K_FLAG_QMI_FAIL is set, skipping the
UNREGISTERING set and the reset_work cancel. QMI can also fail during a
recovery boot, while the device's reset work is queued or in its 20 s
wait; the work then runs from destroy_workqueue() in ath12k_core_free(),
after ath12k_core_deinit() cleared ab->ag and the MHI controller was
unregistered, and oopses in ath12k_core_pre_reconfigure_recovery().

Set UNREGISTERING under ag->mutex and cancel reset_work before the
QMI_FAIL test (AHB: run ath12k_ahb_remove_prepare() first).
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ahb.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ahb.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ahb.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ahb.c
@@ -1429,12 +1429,14 @@ static void ath12k_ahb_remove(struct pla
 {
 	struct ath12k_base *ab = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
 
+	/* also on the QMI_FAIL path: see ath12k_pci_remove() */
+	ath12k_ahb_remove_prepare(ab);
+
 	if (test_bit(ATH12K_FLAG_QMI_FAIL, &ab->dev_flags)) {
 		ath12k_ahb_power_down(ab, false);
 		goto qmi_fail;
 	}
 
-	ath12k_ahb_remove_prepare(ab);
 	ath12k_core_hw_group_cleanup(ab->ag);
 qmi_fail:
 	ath12k_core_deinit(ab);
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c
@@ -1705,17 +1705,22 @@ static void ath12k_pci_remove(struct pci
 
 	ath12k_pci_set_irq_affinity_hint(ab_pci, NULL);
 
+	/*
+	 * See ath12k_ahb_remove_prepare(): no reset work queued after the
+	 * cancel. Done before the QMI_FAIL test: QMI can also fail during a
+	 * recovery boot, with this device's reset work still queued or in
+	 * its 20 s wait.
+	 */
+	mutex_lock(&ab->ag->mutex);
+	set_bit(ATH12K_FLAG_UNREGISTERING, &ab->dev_flags);
+	mutex_unlock(&ab->ag->mutex);
+	cancel_work_sync(&ab->reset_work);
+
 	if (test_bit(ATH12K_FLAG_QMI_FAIL, &ab->dev_flags)) {
 		ath12k_pci_power_down(ab, false);
 		goto qmi_fail;
 	}
 
-	/* see ath12k_ahb_remove_prepare(): no reset work queued after cancel */
-	mutex_lock(&ab->ag->mutex);
-	set_bit(ATH12K_FLAG_UNREGISTERING, &ab->dev_flags);
-	mutex_unlock(&ab->ag->mutex);
-
-	cancel_work_sync(&ab->reset_work);
 	cancel_work_sync(&ab->dump_work);
 	ath12k_core_hw_group_cleanup(ab->ag);
 
